{"name": "r-numbat", "id": "68e94c313530c927500ec537", "package_types": ["conda"], "summary": "A computational method that infers copy number variations (CNVs) in cancer scRNA-seq data and reconstructs the tumor phylogeny. 'numbat' integrates signals from gene expression, allelic ratio, and population haplotype structures to accurately infer allele-specific CNVs in single cells and reconstruct their lineage relationship. 'numbat' can be used to: 1. detect allele-specific copy number variations from single-cells; 2. differentiate tumor versus normal cells in the tumor microenvironment; 3. infer the clonal architecture and evolutionary history of profiled tumors. 'numbat' does not require tumor/normal-paired DNA or genotype data, but operates solely on the donor scRNA-data data (for example, 10x Cell Ranger output). Additional examples and documentations are available at <https://kharchenkolab.github.io/numbat/>. For details on the method please see Gao et al. Nature Biotechnology (2022) <doi:10.1038/s41587-022-01468-y>.", "description": "", "home": "https://github.com/kharchenkolab/numbat/, https://kharchenkolab.github.io/numbat/", "public": true, "access": "public", "owner": {"company": "", "location": "", "login": "bioconda", "name": "bioconda", "url": "", "description": "Bioconda is a distribution of bioinformatics software realized as a channel for the versatile Conda package manager.", "created_at": "2015-09-11 22:59:20.880000+00:00", "user_type": "org"}, "full_name": "bioconda/r-numbat", "url": "http://api.anaconda.org/packages/bioconda/r-numbat", "html_url": "http://anaconda.org/bioconda/r-numbat", "versions": ["1.4.2", "1.5.1", "1.5.2"], "latest_version": "1.5.2", "platforms": {"linux-64": "1.5.2", "osx-64": "1.5.2"}, "conda_platforms": ["osx-64", "linux-64"], "revision": 12, "license": "MIT", "license_url": null, "dev_url": null, "doc_url": null, "source_git_url": null, "source_git_tag": null, "app_entry": {}, "app_type": {}, "app_summary": {}, "builds": ["r